{"source_id": "dilg-memo-no-2015-76-early-preparedness-actions-to-reduce-disaster-risks", "file_name": "DILG_Memo_No_2015_76_Early_Preparedness_Actions_to_Reduce_Disaster_Risks.pdf", "page": 3, "extraction_method": "ocr", "line_count": 54, "character_count": 2126, "lines": [{"line": 1, "text": "6.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 2, "text": "Establish", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 3, "text": "partnership with", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 4, "text": "other", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 5, "text": "local government", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 6, "text": "units", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 7, "text": "for DRRM", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 8, "text": "and", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 9, "text": "emergency response initiatives pursuant to IRR Rule 6, Sec. 4 (21) of RA 10121.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 10, "text": "On Building Competencies:", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 11, "text": "7.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 12, "text": "In view of IRR Rule 6, Sec. 4 (5) of RA 10121, ensure the conduct of Community", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 13, "text": "Based", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 14, "text": "Disaster", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 15, "text": "Risk Reduction and Management (CBDRRM)", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 16, "text": "training and", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 17, "text": "simulation exercises, i.e., evacuation drills, in each barangay in order to build their", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 18, "text": "competencies in dealing with disasters.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 19, "text": "8.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 20, "text": "In compliance to IRR Rule 6, Sec. 4 (11) of RA 10121, see to it that the DILG’s", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 21, "text": "Pampamilyang Gabay sa Panahon ng Kalamidad, which contains important", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 22, "text": "information on different hazards and actions to be undertaken pre, during and", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 23, "text": "post calamity, is disseminated to every family in your jurisdiction. Said Guide can", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 24, "text": "be downloaded from Attp:/www.dilg.gov.ph/whatsnew/Pampamilyang-Gabay-sa-", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 25, "text": "Panahon-ng-Kalamidad/275.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 26, "text": "On Prepositioning ofEquipment and Supplies:", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 27, "text": "9.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 28, "text": "Stockpile on basic emergency equipment and supplies, i.e., portable generator,", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 29, "text": "gasoline, potable water, food packs and first aid kits, to ensure easy access to", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 30, "text": "essential needs immediately after a disaster occurs.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 31, "text": "10. Ensure installation of signages or markers in identified hazard and danger zones", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 32, "text": "(ie., flood, tsunami, and landslides) in coordination with the Office of Civil", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 33, "text": "Defense, Dept. of Environment and Natural Resources", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 34, "text": "(for landslide and/or", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 35, "text": "rockfall signage), Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology (for tsunami", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 36, "text": "signage), and the Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical & Astronomical Services", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 37, "text": "Administration (for flood and/or storm surge signage) that implemented the inter-", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 38, "text": "agency program “Hazards Mapping and Assessment for Effective Community-", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 39, "text": "Based Disaster Risk Management (READY Project)”. Refer to AnnexA for sample", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 40, "text": "signages or markers.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 41, "text": "11. Purchase, install and maintain water level and rain gauge stations, in coordination", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 42, "text": "with", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 43, "text": "the", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 44, "text": "Department", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 45, "text": "of", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 46, "text": "Science", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 47, "text": "and", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 48, "text": "Technology-Advanced", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 49, "text": "Science", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 50, "text": "and", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 51, "text": "Technology Institute (DOST-ASTI) and Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical &", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 52, "text": "Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA). However, in lieu of advanced", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 53, "text": "technology, use of indigenous technology proven and tested by the community is", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}, {"line": 54, "text": "also acceptable.", "is_repeated_boilerplate": false}]}
